# Independent source-only Sketch installation review

This work-only review authenticates seven distinct frozen epochs before and after: initial277, negative-review111, corrected188, accepted-review81, browser74, source-plan43 and shared-route51. Their825 payloads plus seven manifests account for832 exact source/evidence files. No original/candidate application code, browser, HTTP request, original helper, native executable, benchmark, profiler or behavioral test runs in this review. The checks execute only standard-library source hashing, recorded JSON/TAP recomputation and proof-metadata guards.

The Archive source plan's661 inert aliases preserve all four main source/review epochs including their negatives and manifests. Every destination gains precisely one `.snapshot` suffix and resolves to the declared original path. The eight live proposals are two replacements and six additions; current14 baseline images authenticate exactly, with the two replaced current files additionally captured here and all six additions still absent. Five disclosed adapters reconstruct byte-exact proposals from frozen corrected188 origins. They change runtime/oracle imports, source authentication and owned observation locations; fixture/assertion/original slice bodies remain unchanged. The source census is prospective30 focused/39 expanded/11 new groups; independent fresh78 comparisons are historical and not recounted or newly installed. Syntax checks in Archive's source plan are recorded history, not new execution by this reviewer.

Selected original authority is Excalidraw0.18.1 commit `a2ec2889babf7d2295469c6d90ebe77fae57df84`, eight pinned official source/license files, MIT. URLs, byte counts, digests and exact license map through the correction aliases. The verification-only oracle's literal provenance/release/commit/row/Node executable guards and exact reconstruction were inspected, not evaluated. Its seven source slices provide eight declaration bodies across five source units (alignment also retains `calculateTranslation`). Original dependency adapters and type/module stripping remain explicit. This establishes no complete original renderer/binding/text/frame/rotation/native GUI equivalence. Client/runtime never import the oracle. Current source159 IDs/SHAs and capability232 IDs remain unchanged.

The root51 route adds precisely99 bytes to the static map; removing that one line reconstructs the old807 host exactly, while the corrected host is85fe. Existing loopback, Host, Origin and GET-only guards precede the fixed-file route, which exposes no arbitrary pathname. Recorded TAP preserves first0/2 (real404 and Node-fetch overridden-Host premise), corrected-premise baseline1/2 and route2/2; both controlled10-source intervals are exact. The encoded dot-segment probe uses fetch and may be normalized before transmission, so it is a finite fetch-path denial rather than raw-wire encoded-path proof. The child independently read/authenticated root51 without execution or artifacts and reported no blocking source flaw; this review also authenticates the same bytes and raw observations directly.

The own prior browser74 epoch is unchanged and reviewed as prior author-owned browser evidence, not an independent fresh browser campaign. Recorded checks recompute eight controls and each Undo/Redo, actual group selection/offsets, two no-op histories, real held-pointer keyboard refusal before mutation/release, Save/New/reload/fresh-list reopen and native response geometry. Counts are14 finite groups,68 DOM observations,20 HTTP requests/5 API (3 list/1 Save/1 export),9 correctly labeled JPEGs. Normal owned tab/host/relay/temp cleanup and all10 fresh before/after source rows remain exact. The private7853/cfbf statement-insertion host inverses to old7741/807 and is distinct from root's7840/85fe staticMap route. Native HTTP/document response passes; downloaded-file delivery remains false/unverified following a retained bridge timeout and empty/truncated scoped events. JPEGs pair with DOM/HTTP/disk records and do not expand appearance or universal compatibility claims. Initial prototype assertion, v1 finalizer envelope assertion, optional absent error-log shell read and bridge timeout remain in browser74.

`proof-dataset.json` is a prospective832-alias/10-current dataset under root-confirmed prefixes:661 core aliases,75 browser files,44 source-plan files and52 shared-route files. Current10 means eight app proposals plus root's server and route test. `proof-verifier.mjs` enforces exact bytes, seven complete alias prefixes, safe relative paths and no symlink traversal; `public-proof-loader.mjs` requires an independently supplied frozen dataset digest. Root must pin that digest and the module sources in its authority, then use the loader against the installed repository. The positive staging check reads exact source bytes through an owned in-memory alias map; it is not public-filesystem installation acceptance. Eight negative metadata cases reject traversal, duplicates, wrong source/current digests, scope promotion, prefix omission, extra alias and missing/truncated bytes. Two loader controls reject changed dataset bytes and wrong authority digest. No app acceptance is inferred from these metadata checks.

Root owns all copies, current source interval tests, host route installation and publication. This review preserves before images and recommends the exact source-only plan/route for that next step. Installed behavior, full product/GUI parity, universal correctness, reliability/performance superiority and downloaded-file acceptance remain unestablished.
